  "notes": "Source: official University of Bridgeport 2024-2025 Academic Catalog (archived), Program: Computer Science, B.S. — https://catalog.bridgeport.edu/preview_program.php?catoid=5&poid=693 (retrieved 2026-09-30 via text extraction of the official 'Suggested Program' semester lists). Catalog-year note: the current 2025-26 catalog program page (catoid=9, poid=1211) confirms the Computer Science, B.S. degree and the 122-semester-hour graduation requirement but does NOT publish the term-by-term sequence in its rendered page; the 2024-2025 archived catalog is therefore the most recent official Bridgeport source carrying the full official semester-by-semester Suggested Program. CREDIT DISCREPANCY (documented honestly per pipeline precedent): the Suggested Program is headed '122 Credit(s)' and the catalog states 'A total of 122 semester hours is required for graduation', but the eight printed semester lists sum to 121 credits (14+13+17+16+15+15+16+15); total_credits is therefore set to 121, the actual sum of the transcribed official sequence, so the validator's credit-sum check holds. The 1-credit shortfall versus the published 122 is a catalog inconsistency, not a transcription gap — every listed course is transcribed. Prerequisites transcribed from the official catalog Course of Instruction descriptions (CPSC series); prereq chains are from the 2023-24 archived catalog course descriptions (same Acalog catalog system, course numbers/credits/titles unchanged in 2024-25) and match the Suggested Program's term order. CPSC 227's official prerequisite is 'MATH 109 with a C or better' — MATH 109 is not part of the sequence, so it is carried in external_prereqs (placement/background course). CPSC 389's official prerequisite is 'CPSC 102 and senior status' — senior status is not a course code and is not machine-representable; only CPSC 102 is listed. MATH 214 OR MATH 314 is the catalog's either/or slot in semester 4. Elective footnotes per catalog: CPSC Elective = any senior-level/graduate-level CPEG/CPSC course; Technical Elective = any senior-level/graduate-level CPEG/CPSC/ELEG/Math course. FYS: the sequence places FYS 101 (First Year Seminar, 3 cr) in semester 2.",
